Restricted local Linux USB/IP helper; never starts usbipd or creates encryption

Usage: rustusb-helper [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --config <CONFIG>
          Root-owned, non-writable-by-others policy file [default: /etc/rustusb/policy.json]
      --socket <SOCKET>
          Socket in a root-owned, non-writable-by-others directory [default: /run/rustusb/control.sock]
      --physical-state-dir <PHYSICAL_STATE_DIR>
          Root-only persistent physical grant journal, kept across helper restarts [default: /var/lib/rustusb/physical]
      --native-state-dir <NATIVE_STATE_DIR>
          Separate root-only secure Native channel intents, retained across restarts [default: /var/lib/rustusb/native]
      --log-directory <LOG_DIRECTORY>
          Write bounded sanitized NDJSON to an existing root-owned mode0700 directory
      --log-max-bytes <LOG_MAX_BYTES>
          Maximum bytes per segment; requires --log-directory
      --log-retain <LOG_RETAIN>
          Total retained segments including active
      --log-json
          Use JSON stderr tracing in legacy mode; file logs are always JSON
  -h, --help
          Print help
